return {
  summary = "A large custom-ball collection for Red/Blue/Yellow and Gold/Silver/Crystal. Version 0.8.10 redesigns the Gen 2 Ball Case with scrolling, recipe costs, catch effects and clear readiness instead of availability dashes. Includes Kurt's full-pocket handover fix.",
  author = "Mister Miracle",
  tags = { "balls", "items", "template", "gold", "crafting", "apricorns" },
  differences = {
    "CAGE BALL (quest/dev only): 1x on its first throw, 2x after one failed Cage Ball, then guaranteed after two failures in the same battle.",
    "CRYSTAL BALL (quest/dev only): plain catch odds. On Gen 2 the catch is followed by a two-page details/moves review; on Gen 1 there is no review -- the screen cannot be loaded there -- and its item description says so instead of promising one. KEEP is default; confirmed RELEASE refunds the ball first and removes only the exact newly caught party/box record.",
    "STRANGE BALL (quest/dev only): independently chooses 0.75x, 1x, 1.5x or 2x on each real throw using battle RNG. ORIGIN BALL (quest/dev only): guaranteed wild catch for a fateful encounter.",
    "GEN 2 CANON SET: Quick (4x on turn 1), Timer (grows to 4x), Net (3x on WATER/BUG), Dusk (3x at night or in caves), Repeat (3x on a previously caught species), Dream (4x on sleep) and Dive (3x while fishing or surfing). Each costs 1000 at Great/Ultra marts and has a two-line mart description.",
    "LUXURY BALL (3000, both games): plain catch odds; on Gen 2 the catch starts at 120 happiness. CHERISH BALL: plain odds, never sold; Kurt gives one after the BALL CASE is safely added.",
    "BALL CASE (Gold/Silver/Crystal): a key item Kurt gives you when you return to him from the Slowpoke Well. Use it from the pack to open a workbench that mixes Apricorns into balls, and to STOW ALL / TAKE BACK this mod's balls. A full pack returns what fits and keeps the rest -- nothing is lost. Apricorns and the case itself are never stowed.",
    "KECLEON BALL (craft: 1 Green + 1 Red Apricorn): 1.5x, the same as a Great Ball, and the ball takes the wild Pokemon's OWN palette as it flies -- pink at a Wigglytuff, red at a Scizor, shiny at a shiny. Cheapest recipe in the tier.",
    "DRIFT BALL (craft: 1 White + 1 Yellow Apricorn): 4x on light, airy species, read off the dex weight.",
    "SNARE BALL (craft: 2 Black Apricorns): catches a sleeping or frozen target outright; an outright dud on anything awake.",
    "CATALYST BALL (craft: 1 Green + 1 Yellow Apricorn): 4x on species that evolve with a stone.",
    "CRADLE BALL (craft: 1 White + 1 Pink + 1 Green + 1 Red Apricorn): never misses, and the catch restarts at level 1 with level-1 moves. DVs and stat experience are kept, so it ends up stronger at 100 than a late catch -- the recipe IS the balance.",
    "ACE BALL: a case recipe that stays hidden until another mod writes save.recipeUnlocks['route_aces:ace_ball']. Not obtainable on its own; ships inert.",
    "BEAST BALL and the four quest-artifact balls are behind [DEV] CHEAP BALLS and registered on every boot. The throwable GS BALL follows that rule in every game except Crystal, whose native GS Ball remains an untouched story key item.",
    "Bag capacity grows by one slot per OBTAINABLE ball. Gen 2: +20 with the canon set, or +13 when its seven shared ids are deferred. Gen 1: +8 to the ITEM bag. [DEV] CHEAP BALLS adds +6, except Crystal adds +5 because the native GS Ball is not sold. It is additive over other capacity changes; VANILLA BAG LIMITS keeps the stock cap.",
    "PREMIER BALL: not sold; buy 10+ balls in one purchase and the clerk throws in one free per 10 (buy 20, get 2). Announced in the shop text on Gen 1; arrives silently in the BALLS pocket on Gold. Plain 1x catch odds.",
    "NEST BALL (1000): better against low-level targets -- 4x at Lv15 or under, 3x at 25, 2x at 35, 1x above. Sold at the Great/Ultra marts.",
    "MOON BALL (1200): Gen 1 only -- 4x against species that evolve by Moon Stone. Sold at Pewter Mart, before Mt. Moon. Gold has its own native Moon Ball.",
    "HEAL BALL (300): normal odds; the caught Pokemon arrives fully healed (HP, status, PP). Sold at the Great/Ultra marts.",
    "FAST BALL (1000): Gen 1 only -- 4x against species with base Speed 100 or higher. Sold at the Great/Ultra marts. Gold has its own native Fast Ball.",
    "MIRROR BALL (1200): 4x when the wild Pokemon is the same species as the one you have out. Sold at the Great/Ultra marts.",
    "SILPH BALL (9800): an abandoned Master Ball prototype -- a guaranteed catch, except one throw in TWO fizzles and the ball is spent anyway. Sold at Saffron Mart on Gen 1 and at Ultra-tier marts on Gold, where it is labelled PROTO BALL; intended to become a one-off quest reward.",
    "Every catch is marked with mon.caughtBall (as a fallback where pokeball_colors owns the field).",
    "Called Kanto Balls until 0.4.3 -- display name only, the id is still kanto_balls and updates carry over. Before that it was Example Balls (mod id example_balls, a real id change, remove that one if present).",
  },
  credits = { "Mart-shelf mechanism follows Custom Poke Balls by magalvao (github.com/magalvao/custom-pokeballs)." },
  compat = {
    "No dependencies. The purchase detection behind the Premier bonus was the separate shop_events mod until 0.6.0 and now lives here; it still EMITS shop.purchased on the same bus, so any other mod listening for it keeps working. If the standalone shop_events is still installed this mod defers to it rather than wrapping Bag.add/Sound.play a second time, which would award the bonus twice.",
    "Runs on Gen 1 (Red/Blue/Yellow) and every Gen 2 game (Gold/Silver/Crystal). Gold/Silver/Crystal are explicit runtime-test fixtures, including their different GS Ball ownership and their different Kurt scripts. Kurt's house holds TWO SPRITE_KURT objects in every Gen 2 game -- one shared script key on Gold/Silver, two different ones on Crystal -- and the case handover matches any of them.",
    "Optional: pokeball_colors, on BOTH generations. Gen 1: this mod owns its ball records AND their colors, and registers them on game.ready; Pokeball Colors must not carry entries for these ids.",
    "Gen 2: this mod owns the THROW colour (its own battleObjects palettes plus a BattleState:ballPalette wrap) and Pokeball Colors 0.1.22+ owns the POKEMON CENTER heal machine, reading each ball's colour back out of ballPalette/battleObjects and the mon.caughtBall mark. The two do not overlap. Other ball mods should call exports.registerBallPalette(ballId, paletteName, row) instead of adding a second wrap; that also gets them onto the heal machine. Native MOON and FAST BALL colours, plus Crystal's native GS Ball, are left alone.",
    "Optional: Custom Poke Balls intentionally owns QUICK/TIMER/NET/DUSK/REPEAT/DREAM/DIVE on Gen 1. Too Many Balls owns those ids on Gen 2 unless a Gen 2 build of Custom Poke Balls is loaded or CANON BALL SET is off. Turning the set off while holding one leaves a raw item in ITEMS until re-enabled.",
    "Changing a mod option takes effect on the NEXT load, not immediately: prices, which balls are registered and which mart shelves carry them are all decided in the entry chunk and nothing re-reads the option afterwards. A full quit and relaunch applies it.",
    "Publishes exports.owns = { kanto_balls = true, balls = { ...ids... } } and exports.balls.",
  },
}
